# Per-model export working dirs. The Python envs and downloaded checkpoints are
# Mac-local and must NEVER sync to the Windows box (scripts/sync uses
# --ignore-vcs, so anything ignored here is skipped by mutagen).
#
# The small ONNX masters + golden .npy tensors under */artifacts/ are NOT
# ignored on purpose: the box replays them on the DirectML/CUDA EPs.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pth
*.pt
*.fp32.onnx

# Vendored upstream model code, cloned at a pinned commit by export.py, which
# re-checks the commit out on every run. Re-clonable, and a nested .git inside
# the tree is not something to commit.
redimnet/checkpoints/

# ReDimNet2-B2 is 15.3 MB (whole-graph fp32 — the mel frontend cannot be fp16,
# see export.py), over the >10 MB rule. `uv run python export.py` regenerates it
# byte-for-byte from the pinned upstream commit, and the Studio CDN serves it.
redimnet/artifacts/redimnet_speaker.onnx

# Video saliency: the untrimmed U^2-Netp download (export.py trims it to the d0
# head and that trimmed master IS committed) and the upstream demo photo that
# gen_goldens.py derives the two committed reference frames from. Both are
# re-fetchable from their pinned URLs.
video_saliency/artifacts/u2netp.onnx
video_saliency/frames/largest_selfie.jpg
